    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Nanette Diaz Barragán is the U.S. Representative for California's 44th District, serving since 2017; she previously was a Hermosa Beach city councilmember from 2013 to 2015. She sits on the House Energy and Commerce Committee.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Nanette Diaz Barragán is the U.S. Representative for California's 44th District, serving since 2017; she previously was a Hermosa Beach city councilmember from 2013 to 2015.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She sits on the House Energy and Commerce Committee.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Her legislative work focuses heavily on environmental justice and air pollution, which she describes as a public health crisis in her district due to freeways, ports, oil refineries and urban drilling. In 2020, she introduced the Climate Smart Ports Act to invest in zero-emissions technology at ports, and the Outdoors for All Act to fund park projects in urban, low-income communities. On health access, she introduced the Improving Social Determinants of Health Act in 2020. In 2026, she introduced the Ensuring Kids Have Access to Medically Necessary Dental Care Act and the 9-8-8 Community Infrastructure Act. Her campaign prioritizes protecting Medicare and Social Security and passing comprehensive immigration reform.",
        "cites": [2, 3, 4, 5],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Her legislative work focuses heavily on environmental justice and air pollution, which she describes as a public health crisis in her district due to freeways, ports, oil refineries and urban drilling.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "In 2020, she introduced the Climate Smart Ports Act to invest in zero-emissions technology at ports, and the Outdoors for All Act to fund park projects in urban, low-income communities.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "On health access, she introduced the Improving Social Determinants of Health Act in 2020.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "In 2026, she introduced the Ensuring Kids Have Access to Medically Necessary Dental Care Act and the 9-8-8 Community Infrastructure Act.",
            "cites": [4]
          },
          {
            "text": "Her campaign prioritizes protecting Medicare and Social Security and passing comprehensive immigration reform.",
            "cites": [5]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Barragán voted to impeach President Trump for incitement of insurrection in 2021. In 2020, she voted for the Moving Forward Act, a more than $1.5 trillion infrastructure package that included her port and parks bills.",
        "cites": [6, 3],
